<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sistine Chapel ceiling</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1508">1508</a>–<a href="/years/1512">1512</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michelangelo">Michelangelo</a> painted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sistine-chapel">Sistine Chapel</a> ceiling between 1508 and 1512 for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-julius-ii">Pope Julius II</a>, with nine scenes from Genesis, prophets, sibyls and the ancestors of Christ.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sistine-chapel-ceiling.jpg" alt="Sistine Chapel ceiling" width="330" height="119" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michelangelo · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CAPPELLA_SISTINA_Ceiling.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>His works include the David, the <b>Sistine Chapel ceiling</b> and the Last Judgement.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/february-18">18 February in history</a></li></ul></section>
